WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:13.930
And it faces the main road 
to Jerusalem.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:18.518
This is a story about 
what happened here in 1948.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.812
We are only 750 people. 

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:22.147
And everybody knows each other.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.948
It was a black spot in the history.

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:34.576
That history has been
carefully concealed...

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:38.997
purposefully distorted, and in the West, 
largely forgotten.

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:43.585
They put our village as an example
of what they can do.

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:46.171
The massacre in this village
was one of many

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.173
in a series of catastrophic events...

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.425
that became known as 
the Nakba.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.385
When hundreds of thousands 
of Palestinians

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.554
were violently displaced 
from their homeland...

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.515
in order to create 
the state of Israel.

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:03.396
“In May of 1948, a new Jewish state

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.774
Israel was born in a bath of blood.”

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:09.569
The borders of Palestine have been 
changed forcefully over time.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:13.239
But historically, this region has been home 
to Palestinians for centuries

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.450
with hundreds of villages and thriving cities.

00:01:15.992 --> 00:01:18.036
One of them being the central city 
of Jerusalem...

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:20.246
with holy sites important to Jewish

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.123
Christian and Muslim people.

00:01:22.832 --> 00:01:25.919
By the late Ottoman Empire, 
Palestinians living here

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.378
were overwhelmingly Muslim 

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:30.340
with minority Christian and 
Jewish native populations, too.

00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:32.050
But regardless of religion

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.677
Palestinians were often 
referred to as Arabs.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.055
People of the Arabic speaking world

00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:38.765
despite their distinctive culture.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:42.727
Palestinians have long distinguished 
themselves as Ahl Filastīn...

00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:44.604
or the people of Palestine.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.440
They developed a distinctive 
Arabic accent.

00:01:47.565 --> 00:01:51.528
They developed regional food, regional dress, 
and family ties.

00:01:52.153 --> 00:01:54.280
But by the time World War I began...

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:56.116
several key political forces

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.243
were competing for control of these lands.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.746
First, there was a growing Arab 
political movement...

00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:04.457
looking for independence from 
the Ottoman Empire

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:07.377
in hopes of a unified Arab state 
that would include Palestine.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.879
Then there were Zionists

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:12.298
a political group that had one main goal:

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.467
The creation of a Jewish state.

00:02:14.717 --> 00:02:17.470
Zionism was a response to 
an increasingly brutal climate

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.348
for Jewish people, particularly 
in Europe and Russia...

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:22.934
where there was a massive wave 
of antisemitism...

00:02:23.059 --> 00:02:27.188
including large scale attacks 
in the late 1800s and early 1900s.

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:30.692
After briefly considering other areas
for a new state

00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:32.610
including Uganda and Argentina...

00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:35.196
Zionist leaders decided on Palestine

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:37.490
because of its connection to early religious history.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.994
But there was a third key group 
with political interests here.

00:02:41.786 --> 00:02:42.620
The British.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.540
Control of the region would 
allow them to expand

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.209
their spheres of influence and protect 
trade routes to India.

00:02:48.626 --> 00:02:50.962
During World War I, since both 
the British

00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:53.715
and the Arab independence movement 
wanted Palestine...

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.384
they decided to go after 
the Ottomans together

00:02:56.384 --> 00:02:58.136
with an important pledge.

00:02:58.136 --> 00:03:00.180
Through a series of letters in 1916

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.390
an Arab leader and a British official agreed

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:05.018
that if Arabs would help the British 
fight the Ottomans

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:08.438
and give the British economic and other 
foreign privileges in Arab lands...

00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:11.983
in return, the British would recognize and support

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:14.027
an independent Arab state.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.862
Soon the Arabs started 
doing their part

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.530
in revolting against 
the Ottomans

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.407
making it easier for the British to move in.

00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:23.119
But the next year the British issued 
a new declaration

00:03:23.119 --> 00:03:24.662
and betrayed the Arabs.

00:03:27.123 --> 00:03:30.585
“In 1917, Lord Allenby conquered 
the Holy Land...

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.713
and the Jews were promised 
a national home in Palestine.”

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:37.175
Without consulting the native 
Palestinian population...

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.386
the British issued what's known as 
the Balfour Declaration:

00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:42.972
Supporting the establishment
in Palestine

00:03:42.972 --> 00:03:45.099
of a national home for 
the Jewish people.

00:03:45.516 --> 00:03:47.977
So instead of supporting 
the idea of Palestine

00:03:47.977 --> 00:03:50.355
as part of a unified and independent 
Arab state...

00:03:50.772 --> 00:03:53.733
the British pledged to help secure this land 
for Zionists.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.902
It was a strategic move.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.321
This declaration opened up a pathway for Britain

00:03:58.321 --> 00:03:59.864
to gain power in Palestine.

00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:01.241
Under the guise

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:04.786
that it was supporting the self-determination
of another people...

00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:07.497
of a people in Palestine...

00:04:07.872 --> 00:04:09.791
who don't reside there yet.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.835
As for Palestine's majority 
Arab population

00:04:12.835 --> 00:04:15.630
the declaration referred to them as 
non-Jewish communities...

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.049
who would be given civil 
and religious rights...

00:04:18.299 --> 00:04:20.218
but not political rights.

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:22.720
A few years later, after World War I ended

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.390
Britain gained control of Palestine 
through a mandate...

00:04:25.723 --> 00:04:28.142
that also required them 
to put the Balfour plans

00:04:28.142 --> 00:04:30.311
for Jewish settlement in motion.

00:04:30.311 --> 00:04:31.354
And they did.

00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:34.023
Between 1922 and 1931

00:04:34.023 --> 00:04:36.025
the Jewish population 
more than doubled.

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:39.028
The migration helped the 
Zionist movement gain steam.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.363
And a slogan took off.

00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:43.992
“A land without people for,
a people without land.”

00:04:44.242 --> 00:04:46.536
And it sends a message to Western leaders...

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:51.249
that the people who had been living 
in Palestine for generations...

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:54.168
could just be easily moved elsewhere.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:58.047
The idea was that those inhabitants 
weren't a people

00:04:58.047 --> 00:05:00.216
with ties to that land.

00:05:00.591 --> 00:05:03.928
Palestine was, of course, 
a land with a people.

00:05:04.053 --> 00:05:07.265
In 1931, there were more than 850,000

00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:10.268
Palestinian Arabs in the region, 
still the vast majority.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.147
But with the rise of Hitler and the Nazi Party in particular...

00:05:14.772 --> 00:05:16.816
“Hate became a rallying call.”

00:05:17.191 --> 00:05:19.694
Jewish flight from Europe 
became even more urgent.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.487
And Palestine started to see

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.656
the biggest wave of Jewish emigration yet.

00:05:24.198 --> 00:05:27.076
Violence broke out, rooted in 
tensions over land.

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:30.163
Jewish settlers purchased 
swaths of fertile land

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.622
and evicted tenant farmers

00:05:31.622 --> 00:05:34.000
creating a crisis of hundreds of thousands

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.086
of landless, dispossessed 
Palestinian-Arabs.

00:05:38.087 --> 00:05:40.089
Though Palestinians fiercely rebelled against 

00:05:40.089 --> 00:05:43.134
both British colonial forces
and Jewish settlers

00:05:43.134 --> 00:05:44.927
they were brutally crushed 
by the British.

00:05:45.136 --> 00:05:47.638
They put in Palestine

00:05:47.638 --> 00:05:50.099
more troops to repress that rebellion

00:05:50.099 --> 00:05:52.310
than they had stationed in India at that time.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:53.519
All of India.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.521
These troops killed thousands 
of Palestinians

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.065
including many of their leaders

00:05:57.065 --> 00:05:59.901
and the British began training 
and arming Zionist militias

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:01.903
to suppress the rebellion, too.

00:06:01.903 --> 00:06:03.571
But the rebellion continued.

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:06.699
So in an attempt to prevent further 
Palestinian resistance...

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:09.786
the British began to limit Jewish immigration 
into Palestine.

00:06:10.661 --> 00:06:12.872
This ended up angering 
Zionist extremists

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.707
leading to more violence.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:18.628
So in 1947, after decades of trying 
to manipulate

00:06:18.628 --> 00:06:22.924
both Palestinian Arabs and Zionists 
to keep their control over Palestine...

00:06:23.341 --> 00:06:24.509
Britain gave up...

00:06:24.842 --> 00:06:28.096
and handed the question of Palestine 
to someone else.

00:06:28.096 --> 00:06:29.347
“To the United Nations

00:06:29.347 --> 00:06:31.599
also came the problem of Palestine.”

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:32.850
“In recent years

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.645
this small country had been the scene 
of disorder and bloodshed.”

00:06:36.437 --> 00:06:39.774
They figured, here is this new thing
called the United Nations. 

00:06:40.191 --> 00:06:41.609
Here. In your lap.

00:06:41.818 --> 00:06:43.694
Palestine. First gift.

00:06:43.694 --> 00:06:46.989
So the United Nations has 
now to figure out

00:06:46.989 --> 00:06:49.659
how do you disentangle 
this thing...

00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:53.037
that the British who helped create.

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:56.624
A UN special committee proposed 
the land be divided into two states...

00:06:56.833 --> 00:06:59.627
a Jewish state and an Arab state, 
with Jerusalem

00:06:59.627 --> 00:07:02.171
as a separate UN-controlled entity.

00:07:02.171 --> 00:07:05.049
It was called the Partition Plan of 1947.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:08.052
The plan shocked Palestinians.

00:07:08.052 --> 00:07:11.055
We could not accept the partition plan

00:07:11.055 --> 00:07:14.934
because at that time the population 
was almost 2 to 1.

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:17.353
But the plan proposed giving over 
half the land

00:07:17.353 --> 00:07:19.856
and often the most fertile areas 
to the Jewish state.

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:22.900
From a purely pragmatic perspective...

00:07:23.526 --> 00:07:27.280
the partition plan didn't make much sense 
for Palestinian Arabs.

00:07:27.655 --> 00:07:29.949
That wasn't the only problem 
with the plan.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:32.160
Within this proposed area of the Jewish state...

00:07:32.535 --> 00:07:34.996
were hundreds of thousands 
of Palestinian Arabs...

00:07:35.204 --> 00:07:39.208
including both Muslims and Christians 
who had lived there for generations.

00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:40.626
On a moral level...

00:07:41.002 --> 00:07:43.546
the idea of making hundreds of thousands

00:07:43.546 --> 00:07:47.383
of Palestinian Arabs minorities 
in their own homeland...

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:50.303
seemed unjust and unfair.

00:07:50.761 --> 00:07:54.599
In November 1947, the UN 
put the plan to a vote.

00:07:54.599 --> 00:07:56.350
In the aftermath of the Holocaust 

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:59.395
and after lobbying from 
US leaders and Zionists

00:07:59.395 --> 00:08:01.939
the UN voted in favor of partition.

00:08:01.939 --> 00:08:05.026
“And finally, a momentous decision 
to partition the Holy Land’s

00:08:05.026 --> 00:08:06.486
10,000 square miles.”

00:08:07.361 --> 00:08:09.822
Britain announced their mandate 
over Palestine

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:12.408
would end on May 15th, 1948.

00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:15.036
Even as Palestinians continued to reject

00:08:15.036 --> 00:08:17.079
the UN's decision to partition the land.

00:08:17.079 --> 00:08:20.291
After the partition took place, 
you know, in 1947...

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:21.876
you know, we really were scared

00:08:21.876 --> 00:08:23.419
that something might happen to us.

00:08:23.419 --> 00:08:25.213
By the end of 1947

00:08:25.213 --> 00:08:28.216
Zionists had several well-developed 
paramilitary forces...

00:08:28.466 --> 00:08:30.510
the largest one known as the Haganah.

00:08:30.718 --> 00:08:33.304
And more extremist militias like Irgun.

00:08:33.429 --> 00:08:37.058
On March 10th, a couple of months before 
the British mandate would end

00:08:37.058 --> 00:08:39.894
the Haganah adopted what was called 
Plan Dalet.

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:41.229
Or Plan D. 

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:45.066
On paper, the main goal was to 
gain control of the Jewish state

00:08:45.066 --> 00:08:47.985
as laid out in the partition plan, 
while also defending

00:08:47.985 --> 00:08:50.446
Jewish settlements outside of the borders.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:54.158
In reality, that's where the majority 
of these operations took place...

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:56.827
outside of the UN's 
proposed Jewish state.

00:08:57.036 --> 00:09:00.790
Some carried out by Haganah and others
by more radical militias.

00:09:00.957 --> 00:09:04.126
Many of these operations focused on
isolating Jerusalem

00:09:04.126 --> 00:09:05.461
and the roads to it.

00:09:05.461 --> 00:09:07.713
A set of brutal instructions called for

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:10.299
the destruction of Arab villages 
by setting fire to

00:09:10.299 --> 00:09:12.677
blowing up and planting mines.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.679
Especially those population centers

00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:16.514
which were difficult to control.

00:09:16.764 --> 00:09:18.015
In case of resistance

00:09:18.015 --> 00:09:20.226
it called for the population
to be expelled

00:09:20.226 --> 00:09:21.727
outside of the borders of the state...

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:23.479
villages emptied

00:09:23.479 --> 00:09:26.691
and for the occupation and control 
of Arab villages

00:09:26.691 --> 00:09:29.110
along main transportation arteries.

00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:32.905
One of the most widely publicized
village massacres

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:34.991
happened here in Deir Yassin.

00:09:34.991 --> 00:09:37.410
We lkived in Deir Yassin

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:41.080
which is about 4 miles west 
of Jerusalem.

00:09:41.414 --> 00:09:43.541
91 year old Dawud Assad

00:09:43.541 --> 00:09:47.086
was there the day of the massacre 
and was 18 at the time.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.230
On April 9th, 1948, extremist 
Zionist forces

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:09.233
executing Plan D closed in 
on Deir Yassin...

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.694
even though the village had made
a local peace pact

00:10:11.694 --> 00:10:13.863
with neighboring Jewish settlements.

00:10:13.863 --> 00:10:15.906
Friday morning they attacked us.

00:10:50.441 --> 00:10:52.443
Dawud escaped through a trench.

00:10:52.443 --> 00:10:55.696
I went down, all the way down here 
like this.

00:10:55.696 --> 00:10:58.616
So about 4 hours walking 
to Jerusalem.

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:03.371
To this day, the archive of the Israeli army 
refuses to release

00:11:03.371 --> 00:11:06.332
many of the images and intelligence reports 
on Deir Yassin.

00:11:06.874 --> 00:11:10.461
But one UN report detailed 
circumstances of great savagery...

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:14.006
including women and children 
stripped, lined up...

00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:16.842
photographed and slaughtered.

00:11:16.842 --> 00:11:20.346
Roughly 100 people, largely children
and the elderly

00:11:20.346 --> 00:11:21.347
were killed in the village.

00:11:21.972 --> 00:11:25.726
As for Dawud, he later reunited 
with the group of Deir Yassin captives

00:11:25.726 --> 00:11:27.687
in Jerusalem, including his sister 
and mother.

00:11:27.978 --> 00:11:29.146
My mother says...

00:11:36.237 --> 00:11:37.738
So everywhere there’s a commotion,
you know?

00:11:47.707 --> 00:11:49.208
News of what happened 
in Deir Yassin

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:51.460
spread quickly with far reaching effects.

00:11:52.128 --> 00:11:55.423
The Zionist militias used it 
as a propaganda tool

00:11:55.423 --> 00:11:57.550
to tell people about it everywhere.

00:11:57.717 --> 00:11:59.802
The idea was that if you don't leave...

00:11:59.969 --> 00:12:02.805
we will do to you what happened 
in Deir Yassin.

00:12:02.805 --> 00:12:05.266
Stories came out about women
being raped

00:12:05.266 --> 00:12:07.017
about babies being killed

00:12:07.017 --> 00:12:12.314
and induced a great deal of fear among 
the Palestinian Arab population

00:12:12.314 --> 00:12:15.025
many of them fleeing as a result.

00:12:15.109 --> 00:12:17.987
“Jewish troops surrounded Arab forces 
from the city of Haifa.”

00:12:17.987 --> 00:12:19.572
After taking Deir Yassin

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:22.450
Zionist paramilitary groups 
cleared major cities

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.410
including Haifa and Jaffa

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:27.496
and took hundreds of smaller 
villages and towns, too.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:30.666
Hundreds of thousands of Palestinians 
were forced to flee

00:12:30.666 --> 00:12:32.877
pouring into neighboring states 
as refugees.

00:12:33.711 --> 00:12:36.338
Plan D became the blueprint 
for carrying out

00:12:36.338 --> 00:12:38.883
the ethnic cleansing of historic Palestine

00:12:38.883 --> 00:12:41.135
to make room for a new state.

00:12:41.135 --> 00:12:44.555
And on May 14th, the day before 
the British mandate ended...

00:12:45.139 --> 00:12:47.641
Zionist declared the state as Israel.

00:13:05.826 --> 00:13:08.454
But the creation of Israel 
didn't end the Nakba.

00:13:08.829 --> 00:13:11.165
Neighboring Arab countries 
that were overwhelmed

00:13:11.165 --> 00:13:14.376
by Palestinian refugees immediately 
went to war with Israel.

00:13:14.585 --> 00:13:16.670
“Now united and a league of Arab States...

00:13:17.087 --> 00:13:19.256
they are insistent that the entry of refugees

00:13:19.256 --> 00:13:21.717
into Palestine must be ended.”

00:13:21.717 --> 00:13:23.594
The fighting lasted for months.

00:13:23.594 --> 00:13:26.138
Arab armies eventually lost, 
while Palestinians

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:29.225
continued to be killed and forced out
throughout that time.

00:13:31.227 --> 00:13:33.646
Palestinians who fled often carried
only enough

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:35.523
to stay away for a few weeks

00:13:35.523 --> 00:13:37.483
hoping they'd eventually return home.

00:13:37.483 --> 00:13:39.610
A lot of them locked their doors

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:43.113
put their key in their pocket
and then moved to safer ground.

00:13:43.197 --> 00:13:45.616
When you leave the house and 
you take your keys with you

00:13:45.616 --> 00:13:47.785
it’s because you're planning to go home.

00:13:47.785 --> 00:13:50.204
In the case of the Palestinians

00:13:50.204 --> 00:13:52.873
those refugees weren't allowed 
to return.

00:13:52.873 --> 00:13:55.251
Refugees trying to return 
were often shot at.

00:13:55.709 --> 00:13:58.754
Zionist paramilitary operations 
also tried to prevent them

00:13:58.754 --> 00:14:01.090
from returning again by destroying 
the villages.

00:14:01.799 --> 00:14:06.512
That act of preventing their return 
compounded the Nakba.

00:14:06.762 --> 00:14:09.640
So the Nakba is both the forcible displacement

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:12.977
of Palestinians from their homes 
and lands and country...

00:14:13.394 --> 00:14:16.146
as well as preventing them to return

00:14:16.146 --> 00:14:18.065
once the fighting was over.

00:14:18.065 --> 00:14:21.485
Palestinian society was 
dismembered, crushed.

00:14:22.486 --> 00:14:24.488
More than half of the 
Palestinian people

00:14:24.488 --> 00:14:29.118
became refugees, stateless, 
dispossessed of their land.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.163
Over time, the state of Israel

00:14:33.163 --> 00:14:37.001
covered up the physical evidence 
of an Arab Palestine.

00:14:37.001 --> 00:14:40.504
Place names were often changed 
from Arabic ones to Hebrew ones.

00:14:40.838 --> 00:14:43.591
The Jewish National Fund 
embarked on a massive effort

00:14:43.591 --> 00:14:44.967
to plant thousands of acres

00:14:44.967 --> 00:14:47.803
of pine forests and recreational areas

00:14:47.803 --> 00:14:50.764
on top of hundreds of ruined 
Palestinian villages.

00:14:51.181 --> 00:14:55.185
Even though these forests have now grown 
into big pine trees

00:14:55.185 --> 00:14:57.646
Palestinians have not forgotten 
their homelands.

00:14:57.688 --> 00:14:59.732
While we know that roughly 
6,000 Israelis

00:14:59.732 --> 00:15:01.567
lost their lives in the violence of the Nakba...

00:15:01.775 --> 00:15:04.194
records for Palestinian deaths 
weren't kept.

00:15:04.612 --> 00:15:07.156
It's estimated to be around 15,000.

00:15:08.365 --> 00:15:09.658
By the end of the Nakba

00:15:09.658 --> 00:15:13.704
roughly 750,000 Palestinians 
had been forcefully expelled...

00:15:14.288 --> 00:15:17.041
and more than 500 villages destroyed.

00:15:18.042 --> 00:15:22.212
Though the UN’s partition plan 
allotted Israel 56% of the land

00:15:22.212 --> 00:15:25.674
through the Nakba, Israel captured
78% of the land.

00:15:26.383 --> 00:15:29.303
It was everything except 
what's now known as

00:15:29.303 --> 00:15:31.305
the occupied West Bank 
and Gaza Strip.

00:15:31.764 --> 00:15:35.351
Today, that's up to at least 
85% of the total area.

00:15:35.684 --> 00:15:37.811
Turning 6 million Palestinians

00:15:37.811 --> 00:15:39.980
into refugees without a homeland.

00:15:40.606 --> 00:15:42.358
It's why around the same time

00:15:42.358 --> 00:15:44.777
that Israelis are celebrating 
Independence Day...

00:15:45.402 --> 00:15:48.197
Palestinians are out protesting 
on May 15th.

00:15:48.739 --> 00:15:52.368
Holding up keys as a symbol 
of the homes they lost

00:15:52.368 --> 00:15:54.286
and the hope to return.

00:15:54.286 --> 00:15:57.706
For them, the Nakba isn't just 
a moment in history.

00:15:58.248 --> 00:16:01.251
It's a catastrophe that never really ended.

